    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Question\n\nI have currently this -->\r\n```lua\r\n      custom_textobjects = {\r\n        c = ai.gen_spec.pair('```', '```'),\r\n      }\r\n```\r\nBut this also selects the `lua` part of\r\n\r\n\\``` lua\r\n-- something\r\n\\```\r\n\r\nI only want to select between \\```+\\<code-name\\> and \\```\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.ai</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have currently this --&gt;</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"      custom_textobjects = {\n        c = ai.gen_spec.pair('```', '```'),\n      }\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">      <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">c</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">ai</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_spec</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">pair</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>```<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>```<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>),\n      }</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But this also selects the <code class=\"notranslate\">lua</code> part of</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">``` lua<br>\n-- something<br>\n```</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I only want to select between ```+&lt;code-name&gt; and ```</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.ai\nQuestion\nI have currently this -->\n      custom_textobjects = {\n        c = ai.gen_spec.pair('```', '```'),\n      }\nBut this also selects the lua part of\n``` lua\n-- something\n```\nI only want to select between ```+<code-name> and ```",
