            "body": "## Treesitter approach\r\n\r\n> [!CAUTION]\r\n> Make sure the `markdown` parser is installed (`:TSInstall markdown`) and treesitter is working correctly.\r\n\r\n> [!TIP]\r\n> - Use `:InspectTree` to view the parsed syntax tree for the file.\r\n> - Use `:EditQuery` to test the captures shown below.\r\n\r\n### 1. Define captures for `mini.ai`\r\n\r\n```scm\r\n; after/queries/markdown/textobjects.scm\r\n\r\n; extends\r\n\r\n((fenced_code_block) @code_block.outer)\r\n((code_fence_content) @code_block.inner)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 2. Extend `mini.ai` for the `markdown` filetype\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- after/ftplugin/markdown.lua\r\n\r\nif MiniAi then\r\n  vim.b.miniai_config = {\r\n    custom_textobjects = {\r\n      c = MiniAi.gen_spec.treesitter({ a = \"@code_block.outer\", i = \"@code_block.inner\" }),\r\n    },\r\n  }\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote there is no \"inline\" fenced code block. An error will be thrown for cases like:\r\n\r\n````\r\n```lua name ```\r\n````\r\n\r\n## Pattern approach (preferred)\r\n\r\n`MiniAi.gen_spec.pair` is not intended to be used with lua patterns, so instead we need to define a custom one. As in the previous example, this extends `mini.ai` for the `markdown` filetype and assumes that you have already called `MiniAi.setup()` in your configuration.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- after/ftplugin/markdown.lua\r\n\r\nif MiniAi then\r\n  vim.b.miniai_config = {\r\n    custom_textobjects = {\r\n      c = { \"```%w*().*()```\" },\r\n    },\r\n  }\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe downside is that newlines (`\\n`) are included in the inner match, causing the code block to collapse into a single line:\r\n\r\n````\r\n```lua\r\n|code block -> becomes -> ```lua|```\r\n```\r\n````\r\n\r\nYou can fix this by using a slightly more complex pattern, like:\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> See the comment below for a better pattern implementation.\r\n\r\n<details open><summary>New!</summary>\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.b.miniai_config = {\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    -- Better for `dic`: place cursor where `treesitter` approach does\r\n    c = { { \"```.*\\n().*()```\", \"```().*()```\" } },\r\n    -- Better for `cic`: leave an empty line\r\n    c = { { \"```.*\\n().*()\\n.*```\", \"```().*()```\" } },\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n</summary>",
            "bodyHTML": "<h2 dir=\"auto\">Treesitter approach</h2>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-caution\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-stop mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4.47.22A.749.749 0 0 1 5 0h6c.199 0 .389.079.53.22l4.25 4.25c.141.14.22.331.22.53v6a.749.749 0 0 1-.22.53l-4.25 4.25A.749.749 0 0 1 11 16H5a.749.749 0 0 1-.53-.22L.22 11.53A.749.749 0 0 1 0 11V5c0-.199.079-.389.22-.53Zm.84 1.28L1.5 5.31v5.38l3.81 3.81h5.38l3.81-3.81V5.31L10.69 1.5ZM8 4a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v3.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-3.5A.75.75 0 0 1 8 4Zm0 8a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z\"></path></svg>Caution</p><p dir=\"auto\">Make sure the <code class=\"notranslate\">markdown</code> parser is installed (<code class=\"notranslate\">:TSInstall markdown</code>) and treesitter is working correctly.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-tip\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-light-bulb mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M8 1.5c-2.363 0-4 1.69-4 3.75 0 .984.424 1.625.984 2.304l.214.253c.223.264.47.556.673.848.284.411.537.896.621 1.49a.75.75 0 0 1-1.484.211c-.04-.282-.163-.547-.37-.847a8.456 8.456 0 0 0-.542-.68c-.084-.1-.173-.205-.268-.32C3.201 7.75 2.5 6.766 2.5 5.25 2.5 2.31 4.863 0 8 0s5.5 2.31 5.5 5.25c0 1.516-.701 2.5-1.328 3.259-.095.115-.184.22-.268.319-.207.245-.383.453-.541.681-.208.3-.33.565-.37.847a.751.751 0 0 1-1.485-.212c.084-.593.337-1.078.621-1.489.203-.292.45-.584.673-.848.075-.088.147-.173.213-.253.561-.679.985-1.32.985-2.304 0-2.06-1.637-3.75-4-3.75ZM5.75 12h4.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-4.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5ZM6 15.25a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75h2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75Z\"></path></svg>Tip</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Use <code class=\"notranslate\">:InspectTree</code> to view the parsed syntax tree for the file.</li>\n<li>Use <code class=\"notranslate\">:EditQuery</code> to test the captures shown below.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">1. Define captures for <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code></h3>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-scheme notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"; after/queries/markdown/textobjects.scm\n\n; extends\n\n((fenced_code_block) @code_block.outer)\n((code_fence_content) @code_block.inner)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">;</span> after/queries/markdown/textobjects.scm</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">;</span> extends</span>\n\n((fenced_code_block) @code_block.outer)\n((code_fence_content) @code_block.inner)</pre></div>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">2. Extend <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code> for the <code class=\"notranslate\">markdown</code> filetype</h3>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- after/ftplugin/markdown.lua\n\nif MiniAi then\n  vim.b.miniai_config = {\n    custom_textobjects = {\n      c = MiniAi.gen_spec.treesitter({ a = &quot;@code_block.outer&quot;, i = &quot;@code_block.inner&quot; }),\n    },\n  }\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> after/ftplugin/markdown.lua</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniAi</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">miniai_config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">c</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniAi</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_spec</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">treesitter</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">a</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>@code_block.outer<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">i</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>@code_block.inner<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}),\n    },\n  }\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note there is no \"inline\" fenced code block. An error will be thrown for cases like:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"```lua name ```\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">```lua name ```\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Pattern approach (preferred)</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniAi.gen_spec.pair</code> is not intended to be used with lua patterns, so instead we need to define a custom one. As in the previous example, this extends <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code> for the <code class=\"notranslate\">markdown</code> filetype and assumes that you have already called <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniAi.setup()</code> in your configuration.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- after/ftplugin/markdown.lua\n\nif MiniAi then\n  vim.b.miniai_config = {\n    custom_textobjects = {\n      c = { &quot;```%w*().*()```&quot; },\n    },\n  }\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> after/ftplugin/markdown.lua</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniAi</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">miniai_config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">c</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>```%w*().*()```<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n    },\n  }\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The downside is that newlines (<code class=\"notranslate\">\\n</code>) are included in the inner match, causing the code block to collapse into a single line:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"```lua\n|code block -&gt; becomes -&gt; ```lua|```\n```\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">```lua\n|code block -&gt; becomes -&gt; ```lua|```\n```\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">You can fix this by using a slightly more complex pattern, like:</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-info mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z\"></path></svg>Note</p><p dir=\"auto\">See the comment below for a better pattern implementation.</p>\n</div>\n<details open=\"\"><summary>New!</summary>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.b.miniai_config = {\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    -- Better for `dic`: place cursor where `treesitter` approach does\n    c = { { &quot;```.*\\n().*()```&quot;, &quot;```().*()```&quot; } },\n    -- Better for `cic`: leave an empty line\n    c = { { &quot;```.*\\n().*()\\n.*```&quot;, &quot;```().*()```&quot; } },\n  },\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">miniai_config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Better for `dic`: place cursor where `treesitter` approach does</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">c</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>```.*<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\n</span>().*()```<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>```().*()```<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>} },\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Better for `cic`: leave an empty line</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">c</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>```.*<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\n</span>().*()<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\n</span>.*```<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>```().*()```<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>} },\n  },\n}</pre></div>\n</details>",
            "bodyText": "Treesitter approach\nCautionMake sure the markdown parser is installed (:TSInstall markdown) and treesitter is working correctly.\n\nTip\n\nUse :InspectTree to view the parsed syntax tree for the file.\nUse :EditQuery to test the captures shown below.\n\n\n1. Define captures for mini.ai\n; after/queries/markdown/textobjects.scm\n\n; extends\n\n((fenced_code_block) @code_block.outer)\n((code_fence_content) @code_block.inner)\n2. Extend mini.ai for the markdown filetype\n-- after/ftplugin/markdown.lua\n\nif MiniAi then\n  vim.b.miniai_config = {\n    custom_textobjects = {\n      c = MiniAi.gen_spec.treesitter({ a = \"@code_block.outer\", i = \"@code_block.inner\" }),\n    },\n  }\nend\nNote there is no \"inline\" fenced code block. An error will be thrown for cases like:\n```lua name ```\n\nPattern approach (preferred)\nMiniAi.gen_spec.pair is not intended to be used with lua patterns, so instead we need to define a custom one. As in the previous example, this extends mini.ai for the markdown filetype and assumes that you have already called MiniAi.setup() in your configuration.\n-- after/ftplugin/markdown.lua\n\nif MiniAi then\n  vim.b.miniai_config = {\n    custom_textobjects = {\n      c = { \"```%w*().*()```\" },\n    },\n  }\nend\nThe downside is that newlines (\\n) are included in the inner match, causing the code block to collapse into a single line:\n```lua\n|code block -> becomes -> ```lua|```\n```\n\nYou can fix this by using a slightly more complex pattern, like:\nNoteSee the comment below for a better pattern implementation.\n\nNew!\nvim.b.miniai_config = {\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    -- Better for `dic`: place cursor where `treesitter` approach does\n    c = { { \"```.*\\n().*()```\", \"```().*()```\" } },\n    -- Better for `cic`: leave an empty line\n    c = { { \"```.*\\n().*()\\n.*```\", \"```().*()```\" } },\n  },\n}",
