                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "I'll mark this as the answer, since both approaches indeed work. My personal suggestions:\r\n\r\n- Tree-sitter approach is usually more robust, but in this case it has some weird relations with indentation and leading whitespace.\r\n- I'd go with Lua pattern approach, but a bit more concise and robust (accounts for indented code blocks):\r\n\r\n    ```lua\r\n    vim.b.miniai_config = {\r\n      custom_textobjects = {\r\n        -- Select `ic` as content from first to last non-blank characters\r\n        -- Selection is charwise by default, so common usages are:\r\n        -- - `cic` to \"change inside codeblock\";\r\n        -- - `Vacd` to \"select linewise around codeblock and delete\".\r\n        c = { '```[^\\n]*\\n%s*().-()\\n%s*```' },\r\n      },\r\n    }\r\n    ```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I'll mark this as the answer, since both approaches indeed work. My personal suggestions:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tree-sitter approach is usually more robust, but in this case it has some weird relations with indentation and leading whitespace.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd go with Lua pattern approach, but a bit more concise and robust (accounts for indented code blocks):</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.b.miniai_config = {\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    -- Select `ic` as content from first to last non-blank characters\n    -- Selection is charwise by default, so common usages are:\n    -- - `cic` to &quot;change inside codeblock&quot;;\n    -- - `Vacd` to &quot;select linewise around codeblock and delete&quot;.\n    c = { '```[^\\n]*\\n%s*().-()\\n%s*```' },\n  },\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">miniai_config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Select `ic` as content from first to last non-blank characters</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Selection is charwise by default, so common usages are:</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> - `cic` to \"change inside codeblock\";</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> - `Vacd` to \"select linewise around codeblock and delete\".</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">c</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>```[^<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\n</span>]*<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\n</span>%s*().-()<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\n</span>%s*```<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n  },\n}</pre></div>\n</li>\n</ul>",
                    "bodyText": "I'll mark this as the answer, since both approaches indeed work. My personal suggestions:\n\n\nTree-sitter approach is usually more robust, but in this case it has some weird relations with indentation and leading whitespace.\n\n\nI'd go with Lua pattern approach, but a bit more concise and robust (accounts for indented code blocks):\nvim.b.miniai_config = {\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    -- Select `ic` as content from first to last non-blank characters\n    -- Selection is charwise by default, so common usages are:\n    -- - `cic` to \"change inside codeblock\";\n    -- - `Vacd` to \"select linewise around codeblock and delete\".\n    c = { '```[^\\n]*\\n%s*().-()\\n%s*```' },\n  },\n}",
